<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n72380" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰκούρ-ιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or <i>for housekeeping</i> : hence <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰκούρια</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῶρα</span>), τά, <i>wages,
				reward for keeping the house,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				542
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>keeping within doors</i> : <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰκούρια</span>
			<i>toys to keep children within doors,</i> to amuse them in their
			mother's absence, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				1423.3
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑταῖραι οἰκόριαι</span> (
				Dor.
			 for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰκούριαι</span>)
				<i>female house-</i>mates, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				9.19
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
